2, B2, B3, F2. This gives me:  \nPossible melds: B2 B3 + (B1 or B4) chow (but B4 gone, B1 has 1 left), or W3 pung (needs 1 more W3), or T2 pung (needs 1 more T2).  \nPairs: W3 or T2.  \n\nBetter to keep B234 chow ready and decide pair later.  \n\nSo safest discard: **F2** (only 1 left unseen, less likely to be needed by others, and not helping opponents\u2019 patterns much).  \n\n**Reason:**  \nKeeping B234 chow gives flexibility for a quick win (just need one more tile to complete meld+pair). F2 is a single honor with low probability to complete a pung from my hand. Discarding F2 preserves pairs (W3, T2) and the chow B234. It also avoids breaking a natural meld shape. Safety is moderate since F2 is wind but not prevalent wind (east wind is F1).  \n\n**Answer:** Play F2"}
